<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sin-kashid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sin-kashid was an Amorite king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruk">Uruk</a> in the 19th century BCE, founder of the dynasty that ruled the city independently as the power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isin">Isin</a> declined. He built a palace and restored temples at Uruk, and many of his inscribed bricks and clay cones survive. He married a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumu-la-el">Sumu-la-El</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, a sign of his standing among the Amorite kingdoms.</p></div>
